# Sites that refuse automated link checks but open in a browser: they are
# checked by hand (Daniel and Claude, 2026-09-28), not dropped. The weekly scan
# accepts 403 and 429 already; these fail the checker another way.
# TLS handshake fails in the checker; the page loads
^https?://(www\.)?cipa\.jp/
# resets the checker's connection; the page loads
^https?://(www\.)?hdtvsolutions\.com/
^https?://asterweb\.jpl\.nasa\.gov/
# times out in the automated checker; the page loads in browser
^https?://eprints\.rclis\.org/
# refuses the checker's request (error, no status); the page loads in a browser (Daniel, 2026-10-07)
^https?://(www\.)?globenewswire\.com/
# time out from GitHub's runners (twice on 2026-10-07); both load in under two seconds from elsewhere, checked by script the same day
^https?://bugs\.kde\.org/
^https?://(www\.)?sview\.ru/
# times out from GitHub's runners (twice on 2026-10-07); loads from elsewhere in about five seconds, checked by script the same day
^https?://(www\.)?digitalreviews\.net/
